{title: The Shoot from Jesse}
{subtitle: Isaiah 11:1–2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Cm7] [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A shoot will come up from the [Bb]stump of [Abmaj7]Jesse
From his roots a branch will bear [Cm7]fruit
The Spirit [Abmaj7]of the LORD will rest on [Eb]him
[Abmaj7]Wisdom and un[Bb]derstand[Cm7]ing fill [Abmaj7]his view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Spir[Bb]it of counsel and [Cm7]might
The Spir[Abmaj7]it of knowl[Bb]edge and the [Eb]fear [Bb/D]of the [Cm7]LORD
[Abmaj7]His delight will be [Bb]in the fear of [Eb]the LORD [Abmaj7][Bb]
[Eb]Righteousness and justice are [Abmaj7]his song
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]He will not judge by what his eyes [Bb]see
[Abmaj7]Nor decide by what his ears [Cm7]hear
[Abmaj7]With righteousness he [Bb]will judge the poor
And with [Abmaj7]justice decide [Bb]for the [Cm7]lowly [Abmaj7]of the earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [Bb]Spirit of counsel and [Cm7]might
The Spir[Abmaj7]it of knowl[Bb]edge and the [Eb]fear [Bb/D]of the [Cm7]LORD
[Ab]His delight will be [Bb]in the fear [Eb]of [Abmaj7]the LORD
Righteous[Bb]ness and justice are [Cm7]his song
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Abmaj7]Righteousness will be [Bb]the belt around [Cm7]his waist
Faithful[Abmaj7]ness the sash [Bb]around his [Eb]hips
He [Bb/D]will strike [Cm7]the earth with [Ab]the rod of his mouth
And [Bb]slay the wicked with the [Eb]breath of his lips
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Abmaj7]A shoot from the [Eb]stump of Jesse
A branch [Bb]bearing [Ab]fruit
The Spirit rests [Eb]on him
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
